\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Accumulating the one-step decrease}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{The estimate in \ref{fdip-01DN} applies to an actual potential
whose function and curvature bounds hold. If those same bounds
hold after each exact integration, the quartic coefficient obeys
a scalar relation at every step, with one uniform error constant.
How do its finite accumulated errors compare with
#{g/(1+\beta_p n g)}?}
